    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d194">

                <pb facs="0342" n="254" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg254"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Sir Julian Pauncefote to Mr. Wharton.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-10-12"><hi rendition="#italic">October 12,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 10th instant inclosing copy of a memorial from the Lake
                    Carriers’ Association of Buffalo complaining of discrimination by the Canadian
                    Government against citizens of the United States in the use of the Welland Canal
                    in contravention of article 27 of the treaty of 1871, and to inform you at the
                    same time that I will bring this matter to the attention of my Government.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Julian
                    Pauncefote.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
